## The problem that inspired the business

Imagine someone wants to travel from one city to another. Train tickets may be expensive or unavailable. At the same time, many people are already driving along that route with one or more empty seats.

Two groups have different needs:

- Drivers have spare capacity and may want to share their travel costs.
- Passengers need a ride and may want a more affordable travel option.

The opportunity is to connect them.

A platform can help people discover compatible journeys, coordinate travel, and build trust through profiles, reviews, and other service features.

This is the central business insight behind BlaBlaCar: unused capacity can become useful when the people who need it can find the people who have it.

It is also a useful entrepreneurial lesson because the original insight is not a complicated invention. The value comes from identifying a problem and designing a system that helps people solve it.

