# 6. Two entrepreneurial lessons

These lessons connect the research to the purpose of the showcase.

## Lesson 1: Start with a real problem

Entrepreneurs do not always need to invent something completely new. Sometimes the opportunity lies in observing how people behave and identifying what is missing.

Mazzella's story illustrates this approach: he noticed empty seats during a journey and considered how people travelling along similar routes might be connected.

How to apply this lesson: Before developing an app or website, identify the problem, understand who experiences it, and test whether a solution would actually be useful.

## Lesson 2: Trust and usability are part of the product

A platform that connects strangers must do more than display information. People need enough confidence to use it.

Trust can be supported through clear profiles, reviews, transparent terms, reliable communication, and a straightforward booking process.

How to apply this lesson: When designing a digital product, consider what users need to feel safe and confident, not just what features the developer can build.

These are practical interpretations of the business case, rather than claims that Mazzella has personally stated these exact lessons.

